1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:05,227
HarmonyMate turns a short sung phrase into something you can make together and give to
someone you love.

2
00:00:05,727 --> 00:00:11,739
This is a screenshot walkthrough of the working browser prototype, with a simulated Alexa
Plus experience.

3
00:00:12,239 --> 00:00:19,915
Start with your own unaccompanied phrase. After recording, listen to the preview and choose
to keep it, sing again, or discard it.

4
00:00:20,415 --> 00:00:26,229
A pending take never replaces a kept version. Recording does not automatically mean approval
or sharing.

5
00:00:26,729 --> 00:00:33,600
Choose higher or lower thirds, fifths, or sixths. Each generated harmony becomes an
independent numbered track.

6
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:42,620
The engine estimates pitch and key, then processes the recorded voice locally with ffmpeg.
This is digital signal processing, not an AI singer.

7
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:51,506
Listen to a track alone, or select up to eight tracks to hear together. Adjust their volume
and timing, then save that exact combination as a mix.

8
00:00:52,006 --> 00:00:56,664
Stable track numbers also make conversational requests easier to understand.

9
00:00:57,164 --> 00:01:01,889
To sing a real human harmony, select the tracks you want to hear and put on headphones.

10
00:01:02,389 --> 00:01:09,189
Record while those references play. The microphone is captured separately. Review and keep
the new voice as another track.

11
00:01:09,689 --> 00:01:16,581
Ask what tracks are available, play tracks one and three, or sing with track one. Common
Chinese requests work too.

12
00:01:17,081 --> 00:01:26,336
Thirteen tools cross a real authenticated HTTP MCP boundary. Alexa Plus is simulated in the
browser; there is no live Echo microphone connection.

13
00:01:26,836 --> 00:01:32,772
Save a mix as a musical gift. Review the recipient, note, and fixed version before
confirming.

14
00:01:33,272 --> 00:01:39,112
The recipient can play it in a demo inbox. Later retakes do not change a gift that was
already shared.

15
00:01:39,612 --> 00:01:47,809
The prototype implements recording, independent tracks, harmony processing, mixing,
persistent storage, and confirmed gifts.

16
00:01:48,309 --> 00:01:57,174
Next come listening tests with singers, improved timbre, and official Alexa Plus onboarding.
Hardware latency and live Bedrock use are not verified.

17
00:01:57,674 --> 00:02:04,152
Try HarmonyMate from the public repository. The README includes setup, tests, and the limits
of the demo.

18
00:02:04,652 --> 00:02:07,627
Sing a little. Hear the harmony. Make it together.
